    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d513">

                <pb facs="0986" n="948" sameAs="frus:frus1951v03p1/pg948"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.5/11–3051: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Bruce</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d513-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-11-30T13:00:00+01:00">November 30,
                            1951—1 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3233. In conversation with PriMin
                    Pleven last night I stressed the
                    tremendous importance of getting ahead rapidly with European defense force
                    conference in Paris and bringing its deliberations to a conclusion by Dec. 31. I
                    told him I thought chief difficulty at present was that officials representing
                    the various participating nations needed governmental decisions on outstanding
                    items of disagreement in order to complete their work. He agreed with this and
                    said that as soon as Schuman Plan was out of the way he wld personally take
                    charge of the affair from the French side and press it vigorously to
                    settlement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bruce</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d513-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d513-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was repeated for information to London for Ambassador Gifford, to Rome for the Secretary of State,
                    and to Bonn for High Commissioner McCloy.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
